  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Per Month</p>
  <p class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-100">&mdash;</p>
  <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">no coverage in this range</p>
Real text nodes (not aria-hidden, not sr-only-only, not an image). Sits in
the static summary-tile div (bg-gray-50 light / bg-gray-900 dark, no hover
state on this div). Computed WCAG contrast (relative-luminance formula)
against tailwind.css's resolved rgb() tokens:
  text-gray-800  (31,41,55)   on bg-gray-50  (249,250,251) -> 14.05:1 PASS
  dark:text-gray-100 (243,244,246) on bg-gray-900 (17,24,39) -> 16.12:1 PASS
  text-gray-500  (107,114,128) on bg-gray-50  (249,250,251) -> 4.63:1 PASS (text-xs, needs >=4.5)
  dark:text-gray-400 (156,163,175) on bg-gray-900 (17,24,39) -> 6.99:1 PASS
Both light and dark variants defined on every changed class (grep-confirmed
