--- CHECK 2: "—" placeholders are text content; SR-elaboration judgment ---
Both dashes (kpi-detail.html:50 Per-Month tile, :115 vs-Avg cell) are
literal `&mdash;` text nodes inside `<p>`/`<td>`, not empty elements
styled with a pseudo-element dash or CSS content — confirmed via source
and rendered bytes (`&mdash;` present in the HTML text, not in a `content:`
CSS rule search of tailwind.css). WCAG judgment: the vs-Avg "—" cells carry
no aria-label/sr-only elaboration, but (a) the table's own column header
("vs Avg") identifies what's absent, and (b) the "no coverage in this
range" caption sits in DOM order BEFORE the table, so a linear/virtual-
cursor screen-reader pass encounters the explanation before reaching the
dashed cells. WCAG 2.2 AA has no SC requiring per-cell elaboration of an
already-labeled absent value (1.3.1 Info/Relationships is satisfied by the
column header + preceding explanatory text; 4.1.2 is satisfied because the
cell has real text content, not an empty/unnamed control). Judgment: PASS,
not a FAIL — this is not hidden-text abuse (no content is suppressed from
or injected only for AT) and not color-only signaling (see Check 3).
OBSERVATION (non-blocking): an `aria-label="no comparison, no coverage
this month"` on each dashed `<td>` would be friendlier for a screen-reader
user tabbing cell-by-cell without replaying the whole row, but the
constitution and WCAG are both silent on requiring it — not a FAIL per the
"silent = not your call" instruction.

--- CHECK 3: color-only signaling — none introduced ---
Value cell (kpi-detail.html:113, `.Value`) keeps the same unconditional
text-red-600/dark:text-red-400 class used for every kind's dollar figure —
not conditioned on sign, so color is decorative alongside the always-
present digits. The new dash cells (:50, :115) use a single unconditional
gray class with the "—" glyph as the sole content — no colored/uncolored
branching conveys meaning by color alone. Point 8: PASS.

