--- CHECK 6: hover-state contrast — FAIL, new content, dark theme only ---
The new vs-Avg dash cell (kpi-detail.html:115) is
`<td class="p-3 text-sm text-right text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">&mdash;</td>`
inside a `<tr class="hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-700 ...">` (the
row-hover classes are pre-existing/unchanged on master). This exact color
pairing (text-gray-500 / dark:text-gray-400) does NOT appear anywhere in
master's kpi-detail.html (master's muted-gray pairing is text-gray-600/
dark:text-gray-400, and only ever on label `<p>`s outside any hoverable
row) — it is new content introduced by attempt 2. Computed WCAG contrast
against tailwind.css's resolved tokens, DEFAULT vs HOVER row state:
  light default (white/bg-gray-800 modal bg)      : text-gray-500  -> 4.83:1 PASS
  dark default   (bg-gray-800 modal bg)            : dark:text-gray-400 -> 5.78:1 PASS
  light hover     (hover:bg-gray-50  249,250,251)  : text-gray-500  -> 4.63:1 PASS
  dark hover      (dark:hover:bg-gray-700 55,65,81): dark:text-gray-400 -> 4.06:1 FAIL (<4.5)
On mouse-hover of a no-coverage healthcare month row in dark mode, the "—"
vs-Avg cell's text drops to 4.06:1, below the point-7 (>=4.5:1 normal text)
and point-12 (dark-mode parity — light-hover 4.63 PASSES while dark-hover
4.06 FAILS, an explicit light/dark asymmetry point 12 names as the thing
to catch) thresholds. WCAG SC 1.4.3 does not exempt interactive/hover
presentation states — the text must meet 4.5:1 as rendered in every state
a sighted user encounters it in, and row-hover is reachable by any mouse
user (including low-vision users relying on this exact contrast).
PROVENANCE: attributable to attempt 2. This specific `<td>` and its class
list do not exist in master or in attempt 1's diff (attempt 1 only touched
the .Expenses->.Value rename and the `<th>` label, both already reviewed
and PASSed); the gray-500/gray-400 dash-cell markup is wholly new. Per the
attribution rule ("FAIL only what this task's change introduced or
replicated into new content"), this counts as introduced, not merely
inherited.
OBSERVATION for context, not exculpatory: the immediately adjacent Value
cell in the SAME row (text-red-600/dark:text-red-400, kpi-detail.html:113)
computes even worse on the identical dark-hover background — 3.73:1 — but
that class pairing and the row's hover mechanics are BOTH byte-identical
to master (this exact `<tr hover:bg-gray-50 dark:hover:bg-gray-700>` shape
already wraps the income/expenses/savings/rate kinds' colored value cells
today), so that instance is PRE-EXISTING and out of scope for KD1 — it is
not a KD1 FAIL, only a sitewide backlog item the lead may want to fold in.
A one-line fix for the new cell (swap dark:text-gray-400 -> dark:text-gray-300,
computed 7.00:1 on the same hover background) would resolve K7 for this
specific new cell without touching the pre-existing sibling defect.

FINDINGS SUMMARY
- KD1 attempt-2 FAILURES:
