     "—" cell (kpi-detail.html:115, `text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400`)
     renders at 4.06:1 in dark mode when its row is hovered
     (`dark:hover:bg-gray-700`), below the 4.5:1 minimum for normal-size
     text. Light-mode hover (4.63:1) passes, so this is also a light/dark
     parity break under point 12. New content, not present in master or
     attempt 1.
- OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking):
  1. Pre-existing worse-magnitude analog of the same defect class: the
     adjacent Value `<td>` (text-red-600/dark:text-red-400) in the same
     row computes 3.73:1 on the identical dark-hover background — but its
     classes and the row's hover mechanics are byte-identical to master,
     so out of KD1's scope. Backlog candidate: audit all colored table-row
     cells sitewide for hover-state contrast, not just this diff's cell.
  2. vs-Avg dash cells carry no per-cell aria-label/sr-only elaboration;
     judged acceptable against WCAG (column header + preceding "no
     coverage" text supply context) — a friendliness nice-to-have, not a
